      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "In developed countries, the prevalence of asthma in children has significantly increased in the last decades. However, there is no information about the trends of asthma in Latin America."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "To determine changes in asthma prevalence between 1994 and 2002 in Chilean schoolchildren."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL AND METHODS",
          "content": "The prevalence of asthma symptoms in schoolchildren aged 7 (n =18.697) and 13 years (n =18.939), from South Santiago, Valdivia and Punta Arenas, obtained during phases I and III of the ISAAC, carried out in 1994 and 2002, was compared."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "From 1994 to 2002, the mean national prevalence of \"wheezing in the last 12 months\" in the group aged 6-7 years, changed from 18.2% to 17.9% (p =NS); \"asthma ever\" from 12.5% to 10.7% (p =NS), and \"severe episode\" from 3.2% to 2.8% (p =NS). There was a significant increase of the prevalence of \"wheezing in the last 12 months\", in children aged 13-14 years, from 9.8% to 15.5% (p =0.01); in \"asthma ever\" from 10.2% to 14.9% (p =0.01), and for \"severe episode\" from 2.8% to 3.8% (p =0.01)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "There was a significant increase in the prevalence of respiratory symptoms related to asthma in children aged 13-14 years that was consistent in all the 3 participating centres of the ISAAC. However, the prevalence of asthma symptoms in children aged 6-7 years remained without significant changes between 1994 and 2002."
        }
      ]},
